# Build & Executables
build/
build-release/
bin/
out/

# demo/bin holds the GDExtension manifest, which is source, next to the compiled
# library, which is not. Git cannot re-include files under an excluded directory, so
# un-ignore the folder first and then filter its contents. Without this the
# .gdextension manifest never reaches the repository and a fresh clone cannot load the
# extension at all.
#
# The .dll used to be tracked here. It is a 7 MB build output that changed on nearly
# every commit, and it accounted for 125 MB of the repository's 95 MB history — more
# than twice what the committed release archives cost. CI builds it and publishes it as
# an artifact, and users get it from Releases, so committing it bought nothing. Build
# before running the demo project; the README says so.
!demo/bin/
demo/bin/*
!demo/bin/*.gdextension
!demo/bin/*.uid
.vs/
*.user
*.userosv
*.sln.docstates

# CMake
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
CMakeLists.txt.user
Makefile
*.cmake
!CMakeLists.txt

